      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I can see, only the PTE case can happen in a 4KB mm. `pgd_leaf()` is always `false` on arm64 (the generic fallback in `\u003clinux/pgtable.h\u003e`). THP is off in 4KB VMAs (`vma_thp_disabled()`), so there are no PMD leaves. And contpte is off for 4KB mms (`contpte_is_enabled()`), so every present 4KB PTE reports `PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL`.\n\nWould it be OK to drop the PGD and PMD hunks, and to move the PTE one into a helper in `include/linux/p3s/perf.h`? The upstream walk would then only gain `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM()` and `mm_pmd_offset()`. Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (pte_present(pte))\n\t\tsize \u003d p3s_perf_pte_size(mm, __pte_leaf_size(pmd, pte));\n```\n\nwhere `p3s_perf_pte_size()` returns `mm_pte_size(mm)` for a `PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL` leaf. The walk itself looks right to me: the guard nests, so it\u0027s fine in the NMI path, and `pte_offset_map()` follows it.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "df55c81e4a52798d95acfbe23680c5a9651ddbc5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
